P1–P2 titanium link / FLOW / R2
Units mm. Right-handed; Z up; P1=(0,0); P2=(L,0).
L=42.30346 for A, 37 for B. The horizontal top is Z52.5.
R1=11.25; R2=6.8. At levels (Z, waist half-width)
(22.5,2.85),(29,3),(36,4),(42,4.4),(48,3.85),(52.5,2.8):
  On the positive side use two cubic Beziers with (X/L,Y) poles:
  (0,R1),(.18,R1),(.32,w),(.51,w); (.51,w),(.69,w),(.85,R2),(1,R2).
  Mirror about Y=0. Close each end with its outside semicircle.
  Loft corresponding flanks; cap top and bottom; keep semicircular bosses cylindrical.
Trim underside using a constant-Y extrusion of an XZ curve. Up to X10 keep
Z22.5. Set x2=L-6.8; xm=10+.65*(x2-10). Join (10,22.5) to (xm,32.5),
then (xm,32.5) to (x2,28), by cubic Beziers with horizontal end tangents;
each inner pole is 38% of its segment's X span from the adjacent endpoint.
Beyond x2 keep Z28. Blend both external rims R0.75 before cutting bores.
P1 coaxial bores: Ø17 through, Ø19 × 5 from each end.
P2: Ø9 through. Bearing envelopes at P1: Ø10 ID, Ø19 OD, B5;
lower bearing Z22.5–27.5 and upper bearing Z47.5–52.5.
One stationary spindle, radius/Z range: 4.5/[14,22], 6/[22,22.5],
5/[22.5,58], 4.5/[58,61.7]. Historic upper/lower pilots omitted.
Stock adds 0.30 radially in machined bores and 0.25 axially on bearing
shoulders and local facing lands. The Ø17 internal clearance stays as modelled.
Bearing fits, axial capture and free rotation require verification on the hardware.
